  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Perfect-square trinomial equation — recognise, complete the square, solve</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The height of a structure is modelled by the quadratic equation \[ {@expr@} = 0. \]</p>
<p><strong>a)</strong> Is the left-hand side a perfect-square trinomial?</p>
<div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><strong>b)</strong> Rewrite the equation in the form \((x-a)^2 = 0\).</p>
<div>\( \) [[input:ans2]] \( = 0 \) [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p><strong>c)</strong> Hence find the value of \(x\).</p>
<div>\( x = \) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The coefficient of \(x\) is \({@-2*aa@}\) and the constant is \({@aa^2@}\). Since \(\left(\tfrac{-2\cdot{@aa@}}{2}\right)^2 = {@aa^2@}\) matches the constant, the left-hand side is a perfect square.</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
{@expr@} &= 0\\
(x-{@aa@})^2 &= 0 &&\text{(complete the square)}\\
x-{@aa@} &= 0 &&\text{(square root of both sides)}\\
x &= {@aa@} &&\text{(a single repeated root)}
\end{align*}
\]]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
